Register no Go toolchains

The module registers a toolchain for every Go SDK and host the go_sdk
extension provides, and each build configuration analyses all of them during
toolchain resolution. It is reached only through rules_android, a dependency
of protobuf's Java and Kotlin rules, and nothing in this build resolves a Go
toolchain.

The patch removes two lines from the module's MODULE.bazel and carries the
six around them, too little of the file to attribute.

License: Apache-2.0 (rules_go 0.62.0)

--- a/MODULE.bazel
+++ b/MODULE.bazel
@@ -31,8 +31,6 @@
     "io_bazel_rules_nogo",
 )
 
-register_toolchains("@go_toolchains//:all")
-
 bazel_dep(name = "gazelle", version = "0.51.3")
 
 go_deps = use_extension("@gazelle//:extensions.bzl", "go_deps")
